  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nThe Oxfordshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1898\n£40.00\n\nLow stock, 1 remaining\nThe Oxfordshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1898 quantity\nAdd to Cart\n\nCompiled and Edited by Captain A. F. Mockler-Ferryman\n\nPublished 1899 - Eyre and Spottiswoode, London\n\n \n\nContents:\n\nRegimental Calendar for 1899\nThe Army List January 1898\nThe Army List December 1898\nThe First Battalion in 1898\nThe Record of 1st Battalion 1898\nThe 2nd battalion in 1898\nThe Record of 2nd Battalion in 1898\nThe Depot in 1898\nExtracts from the London Gazette in 1898\nChanges in equipment in 1898\nMusketry 1898\nAthletics in 1898\nFootball in 1898\nCricket in 1898\nThe Polo Cup 1898\nThe 43rd Light Infantry Dinner 1897\nThe 52nd Light Infantry Dinner 1897\nThe North West Frontier Campaign\nOccasional Notes\n\nMiscellaneous\n\nSir John Maxwell Tylden\nSir Martin Hunter's Journal 1778-1783\nThe Diary of a Private Soldier in The Peninsular War\nAlmeida: General Craufurd's Account\nThe Storming of San Sebastian\nSir John Moore's Officers\n52nd Generals 1803-1861\nToulouse: Sir J M Tylden's Journal\nSome 43rd Soldiers\n52nd Officers at Waterloo\nA 52nd Poet\nA Letter from the Falls of Niagara 1838\nSergeant Offord's Journal 1846-1851\nThe 52nd in India 1854-1855\nPresentation of Colours to the 43rd, 1847\nCaptain Hugh Robinson (Norcliffe)\nThe Ranee of Jalaun's Album\nThe New Zealand War\nWar Medals\nMacDonald’s Bridge at Omdurman\nStanding Orders of the Light Division\n\nSome Old Regimental Memorials\n\nNotice to Correspondents\n\nIndex\n\nIllustrations\n\n \n\nPlease Note: Original copies supplied, all in used but reasonable condition. Copy supplied may vary slightly from the one pictured in terms of wear and aging.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nIdentifying Cap Badges: A Family Historian’s Guide\n£25.00 Add to cart\nA True Soldier Gentleman: The Memoirs of Lt. John Cooke 1791-1813\n£3.95 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre XI\n£4.99 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre III\n£5.00 Read more\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
